  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Derivatives reveal where a function rises, falls and curves, and pin down its maxima and minima.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The Mean Value Theorem made visible: the amber secant joins the endpoints, and somewhere between them a tangent (dashed) runs exactly parallel. Slide the right endpoint \\( b \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "canvasId": "apMvtCanvas",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Mean Value Theorem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A curve with a secant line and the parallel tangent guaranteed by the Mean Value Theorem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "apMvtDataBtn",
          "panelId": "apMvtDataPanel",
          "descId": "apMvtDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "apMvtDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points on the curve between the secant's endpoints",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "f(x)",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "apMvtB",
            "label": {
              "en": "Right endpoint <b>b =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 2,
            "max": 8,
            "value": 6,
            "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "apMvtBV",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Right endpoint b",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "apMvtSlope",
            "label": {
              "en": "secant slope",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "amber"
          },
          {
            "id": "apMvtC",
            "label": {
              "en": "tangent at c",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "indigo"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "There is a \\( c \\) in \\( (a,b) \\) with \\( f'(c)=\\dfrac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\) — the ringed point.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Shape of a graph",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Mean Value Theorem</strong>: some \\( c \\) has \\( f'(c)=\\dfrac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\). \\( f \\) increases where \\( f'&gt;0 \\) and is concave up where \\( f''&gt;0 \\). The first- and second-derivative tests classify critical points; optimization finds extreme values.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "MVT",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f'(c)=\\dfrac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Critical points",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f'=0 \\) or undefined",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Concavity",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "sign of \\( f'' \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "2nd-deriv test",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f''&gt;0\\Rightarrow \\) min",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 5.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Classify the critical points of \\( f(x)=x^{3}-3x^{2} \\).</p><p>\\( f'(x)=3x^{2}-6x=3x(x-2) \\), so \\( x=0,2 \\). With \\( f''(x)=6x-6 \\): \\( f''(0)&lt;0 \\), \\( f''(2)&gt;0 \\).</p>\\[ \\text{Local max at }x=0,\\quad \\text{local min at }x=2. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Optimisation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A farmer has 200 m of fencing to enclose a rectangular field with one side along a river (no fence needed there). What dimensions maximise the area?</p><p>Let width \\(=x\\), length \\(=y\\). Constraint: \\(2x+y=200\\Rightarrow y=200-2x\\).</p>\\[A=xy=x(200-2x)=200x-2x^2.\\]\\[A'=200-4x=0\\;\\Rightarrow\\;x=50\\text{ m},\\;y=100\\text{ m}.\\quad A_{\\max}=5000\\text{ m}^2.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Verify the Mean Value Theorem for \\(f(x)=x^3\\) on \\([0,2]\\) by finding the value \\(c\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(f'(x)=3x^2\\). MVT: \\(f'(c)=\\dfrac{f(2)-f(0)}{2-0}=\\dfrac{8}{2}=4\\). So \\(3c^2=4\\Rightarrow c=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt3}=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt3}{3}\\approx1.155\\in(0,2)\\) ✓.",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
